       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day for prescription use, and four times the 1,200 mg/day OTC limit. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury and cardiovascular events go up a lot, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions or pain.\n- **1600 mg per day in divided doses**, such as 400 mg PO four times daily or 800 mg PO twice daily.\n- **400\u2013800 mg PO every 6\u20138 hours as needed**, for pain.\n\nIf 1600 mg four times daily is what you intend, tell me the clinical rationale and I can enter it with a note. Your pharmacy may still need to verify it. Otherwise, tell me which dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it."
      }
